 61GA c  Source produced by {+40}Ca({+24}Mg,3n) (1987Ho01,1978ViZT,1979ViZY).   
 61GA c  1987Ho01 (also 1979ViZY,1978ViZT thesis): E=77-120 MeV {+40}Ca pulsed  
 61GA2c  beam on {+24}Mg target. |DE-E silicon detector telescope               
 61GA2c  shielded system. Observed |e-delayed proton group                      
 61GA3c  with E=3110 {I30} and T{-1/2}=40 ms {I15}. The proton decay mainly     
 61GA4c  feeds {+60}Zn g.s. (<10% to first excited state). A and Z              
 61GA5c  identification is not certain, but it is supported by Coulomb          
 61GA6c  displacement energy systematics. Measured mass excess=-47.73 MeV {I3}. 
 61GA c  2007Bl09: {+61}Ge nuclei produced in a fragmentation of {+70}Ge{++28}  
 61GA2c  beam at an energy of 71.6 MeV using LISE3 facility at GANIL. A nickel  
 61GA3c  target was used. Measured delayed proton events by implanting nuclei   
 61GA4c  in a double-sided silicon strip detector (DSSSD) and isotopic T{-1/2}. 
 61GA c  From RADLIST code, deduced total decay energy is 5500 keV {I400}       
 61GA2c  compared to 13360 keV {I300} from Q(|e) value. The decay scheme is     
 61GA3c  poorly known                                                           
